# Backend Python

- Wire long-lived services only in `app/main.py` lifespan onto `app.state`.
- Read config via `get_settings()`; `Settings` has no `BROKER_MODE` — do not reintroduce MockBroker unless implementing it end-to-end.
- Main HTTP surface is health + TradingView webhook + orders list/get/cancel only. Add routes through existing router patterns.
- Redis is demo-stream only; do not assume Redis on the trading path.
- Durable state goes through Postgres models/repos. OMS HTTP reads are in-memory.
- Current facts: `app/docs/backend-*.md`. Ignore `backend/main.py` (hello stub).
